expr main <([for, to, with, from, of, about, in, on, at, by] you're [help, time, patience, support, understanding, email, message, attention, order, feedback, business, reply, own, family, team, friend, friends, house, home, work, job, car, name, account]), (you're)>

let message "Did you mean `your` (belonging to you)?"
let description "Use `your` for possession; `you're` means `you are`."
let kind "Spelling"
let becomes "your"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "Thanks for you're help." "Thanks for your help."
test "Thanks for you're time." "Thanks for your time."
test "Thanks for you're patience." "Thanks for your patience."
test "Thanks for you're support." "Thanks for your support."
test "Thanks for you're understanding." "Thanks for your understanding."
test "Thanks for you're email." "Thanks for your email."
test "Thanks for you're message." "Thanks for your message."
test "Thanks for you're attention." "Thanks for your attention."
test "Thanks for you're order." "Thanks for your order."
test "Thanks for you're feedback." "Thanks for your feedback."
test "Thanks for you're business." "Thanks for your business."
test "Thanks for you're reply." "Thanks for your reply."
test "Go with you're own plan." "Go with your own plan."
test "Talk to you're team." "Talk to your team."
test "Ask about you're family." "Ask about your family."

allows "Thanks for your help."
allows "You're welcome for the help."
allows "Say hi to your team."
allows "I think you're right."
allows "We know you're busy."
allows "If you're ready, go."
